      sub: 'Steckerbrett: cables that swap letters in pairs',
      sep: ',',
      intro: 'The commercial Enigma, which anyone could buy, had no plugboard. The German army added one in 1930, and it gave the machine more settings than anything else. The plugboard (German: Steckerbrett) is a panel with 26 sockets at the front of the box, below the keys. Every morning the operator plugged cables into it as the daily key said.',
